From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NSControl: -setEnabled: does nothing when the state is
 unchanged

-setEnabled: marked the control for display even when it was already in
that state. NSToolbar validates its visible items after events and each
item's -validate calls -setEnabled:, so every toolbar button redrew after
every event, and that invalidates the views behind it. In MarkdownViewer
on Windows this was about 40% of the CPU per typed key
(danjboyd/ObjcMarkdown#164).

Carried in ObjcMarkdown's Linux and Windows packages; not sent upstream.
AI assistance: this change and this description were written with
Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).
---
 Source/NSControl.m | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/NSControl.m b/Source/NSControl.m
--- a/Source/NSControl.m
+++ b/Source/NSControl.m
@@ -161,6 +161,10 @@
  */
 - (void) setEnabled: (BOOL)flag
 {
+  if ([self isEnabled] == (flag ? YES : NO))
+    {
+      return;
+    }
   [[self selectedCell] setEnabled: flag];
   if (!flag)
     [self abortEditing];
